  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "To the nearest thousandth, \\(\\log_{10}2\\) is \\(0.301\\) and \\(\\log_{10}3\\) is \\(0.477.\\) Which of the following is the best approximation of \\(\\log_5 10?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac87\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac97\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{10}{7}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{11}{7}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{12}{7}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "10/7"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1979-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have \\(\\log_{10}5\\approx1-0.301=0.699.\\) Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\log_5 10&=\\frac1{\\log_{10}5}\\\\ &\\approx\\frac1{0.699}\\\\ &\\approx1.431. \\end{aligned} \\] Of the choices, \\(\\frac{10}{7}\\approx1.429\\) is closest.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(\\log_{10}5=1-\\log_{10}2\\)",
        "Apply change of base, then compare the decimal result with the five fractions"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
